      "writtenOn": "2022-08-09T10:51:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, you are right. But we could argue that only base listening user restriction change to startTethering is wrong because user restricted is only one of factor for tethering supported. Caller should call isTetheringSupported or listen tethering supported callback before using tethering. Just like settings would keep hide if tethering is not supported yet even settings already receive user restricted change.\n\nI would like the keep code as is:\n1. as you mentioned, this is pre-existing.\n2. Settings handle it well, although party code may hate this if they want to re-startTethering when receiving user restriction change without checking tethering supported.\n3. Always base on restricted intent to update supported is more easy to maintain. Otherwise we need to handle the race that restricted result may already take effect in tethering flow before tethering receive the intent and handle it.",
